12. `viable_outcomes_invalid` — `viable_outcomes` lists 3–6 of {fixed_verified, fixed_unverified, workaround, pending_visit, pending_part, pending_customer_test, escalated_open, not_a_fault, abandoned} and fits the problem: `fixed_verified` / `fixed_unverified` only if the fix can be applied during a contact without waiting for a part or a visit, `pending_part` only if the fix needs a part, `pending_visit` only if it needs a technician on site, `not_a_fault` only if the root cause is handling, settings or expectations, `workaround` exactly when `diagnosis_plan.workaround` is set.

